;; A Note is deleted now, not marked done: the button takes the row away and
;; nothing reads it again. So the flag goes, and the Notes already carrying it
;; go with it — those are Notes the owner has dismissed, and simply dropping the
;; column would put every one of them back in his box.
;;
;; **This is the one migration here that loses rows, and the down cannot bring
;; them back.** It restores the column, defaulting every surviving Note to not
;; done, which is what they are; the dismissed ones are gone. Deleting them is
;; the point rather than a side effect — see the commit for why that is the
;; honest reading of "I don't want to keep deleted notes".
{:id "021-drop-note-done"
 :up ["DELETE FROM notes WHERE done = 1"
      "ALTER TABLE notes DROP COLUMN done"]
 :down ["ALTER TABLE notes ADD COLUMN done INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0"]
 :transactions false}
